            <ArticleTitle>The acute presentation of intestinal nonrotation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intestinal nonrotation has been recognized as a cause of obstruction in neonates and children. However, it can also be the cause of significant abdominal pain in adults. The pain is recurrent and often associated with a feeling of distention. If the diagnosis is entertained, it often can be made from basic clinical information.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
